Public License 2.0, either stated in the source script's header or, where the
script states no licence, treated as MPL-2.0 by the owner's decision of 2026-11-28
(such files say so in their docstring). TradingView's House Rules state no default
licence, so for those files this is an assumption, not a grant. Each names
its source script, author and URL in its docstring. MPL-2.0 is a file-level
licence: these files are distributed under MPL-2.0 (https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/);
their source form is this repository. The rest of the package stays under the
MIT License. `tests/test_notice.py` checks that every package file stating an
